  - HH:MM with opens < closes;
  - a known IANA timezone;
  - a positive integer capacity;
  - unique table ids within a restaurant;
  - unique user emails;
  - IDs ≤ 64 characters.
  Do NOT reject seeded bookings for being off-grid, outside hours, over capacity or overlapping. The spec does not say seeds obey booking rules, so leave them tolerated.

Also make sure that a booking created normally always gets a reference that satisfies ^[A-Z0-9]{6,12}$. It does today; keep a unit test that proves it.

