1. YES. GET /x/me [auth] is added: {user_id, display_name, managed_restaurant_ids:[...]} in fixture order, and 401 without a token.

2. Spellings:
- states: NO_GUARANTEE | HELD | CAPTURED | RELEASED | REFUNDED (upper case);
- event types: held | hold_adjusted | captured | released | refunded (lower case, underscore). hold_adjusted.amount_minor is a SIGNED delta;
- next_expected and explanation are always non-empty strings, never null.

3. Errors:
- second hold: 409 invalid_transition;
- wrong-state transition: 409 invalid_transition;
- capture before the start: 409 invalid_transition, with error.message "a no-show can be captured only at or after the booking's start";
- non-manager: 403 forbidden; unknown or not the owner: 404 not_found;
- holding on a cancelled booking: 409 reservation_cancelled;
- key reuse with a different body: 409 idempotency_key_reuse.

4. Shapes (mine first):
- evening:
  - history is a plain ARRAY of the official entries;
  - guarantee is ALWAYS an object (state NO_GUARANTEE when none), never null;
  - everything else is as you wrote.
- notifications: {notifications:[...], reminders:[...]} in CHRONOLOGICAL order (oldest first; reverse it for display). reminders are computed for confirmed bookings starting within 24 h (event "reminder").
- preferences: PUT takes the WHOLE object. Omitted fields reset to defaults, unknown fields are ignored. Too long, wrong type or a bad enum is 422 validation_failed; a non-object or invalid JSON body is 400 malformed_request.
- passport:
  - upcoming, past and cancelled_upcoming are lists of compact Rows {reference, restaurant{id,name}, starts_at_local, starts_at, party_size, table_labels, status, guarantee_state}, NOT full reservation views;
  - counts is {reservations, amendments, cancellations};
  - restaurants_visited is a list of NAMES (strings).
- best-times: the key is best_times, not slots. Items are {rank, starts_at_local, starts_at, free_tables, options, overlapping_bookings, reasons:[text]}, best first, at most 5.
- control-room:
  - reservations[] uses "time" (HH:MM), not starts_at_local, and also has "revision";
  - pressure[] items are {time, booked_seats, total_seats, pressure_percent (int)};
  - policy_in_effect (not "policy") is the accepted_terms shape;
  - guarantees is the totals object {held_minor, captured_minor, released_minor, refunded_minor};
  - outbox is {total, by_state:{...}}.
- guarantees settlement: {restaurant_id, currency, totals:{held_minor, captured_minor, released_minor, refunded_minor}, rows:[{reference, guest, party_size, starts_at_local, state, amount_minor, currency, last_event}]}.
